The FEN tokenizer, the 1968-move action table construction, the win-probability
bucketing, and the bagz record format in chesscore.py follow DeepMind's
searchless_chess code (https://github.com/google-deepmind/searchless_chess),
Copyright 2025 DeepMind Technologies Limited, Apache License 2.0. They were
re-implemented here in numpy/PyTorch and verified equal to the reference on the
real ChessBench data. The ChessBench dataset itself (Stockfish 16 action values
and the Lichess puzzle set) is DeepMind's, released with:

  Ruoss, Delétang, Medapati, Grau-Moya, Wenliang, Catt, Reid, Lewis, Veness,
  Genewein. "Amortized Planning with Large-Scale Transformers: A Case Study on
  Chess." NeurIPS 2024. arXiv:2402.04494.

Stockfish (https://stockfishchess.org) is GPL-3.0 and is not distributed here;
the evaluation scripts call whatever binary you point them at.
